body:
Related: godotengine/godot-proposals#12375
Related: godotengine/godot-proposals#7842
Related: #105750

This PR adds alternative hard-coded non-allocating methods for `PhysicsDirectSpaceState2D` and `PhysicsDirectSpaceState3D` to ensure minimum GC-tracked objects are generated (only for Colliders that are first entering the C# world) when performing a Physics query.

This PR also serves as a proposal to the .NET Team as a potential solution to resolve the long-discussed GC-related issue.

# Approaches taken to resolve the GC challenges:

**Context**: The original method calls `NativeCalls.godot_icall_X_XXX` bridge methods for interop-related operations. The following examples inlined those invocations for better clarity. The new `NonAlloc.cs` alternatives introduced by this PR do not use the bridge methods.

The pro for this PR is that it's the most straightforward and non-intrusive way to implement Non-Allocating APIs. We implement them only at the C# level without modifying the core or touching the binding generator, and the complexity of implementation is merely at the AI doable level.

The con for this PR is that this file is yet another `Compats.cs`, and we need to update it every time their corresponding counterparts are changed manually, and when people decide to implement more and more Non-Allocating APIs, the cost for maintaining will also rise.

## Method that returns a `Dictionary`

Given the following original method:
```csharp
public GodotDictionary IntersectRay(PhysicsRayQueryParameters2D parameters)
{
    var method = MethodBind1;
    var ptr = GodotObject.GetPtr(this);
    var arg1 = GodotObject.GetPtr(parameters);
    ExceptionUtils.ThrowIfNullPtr(ptr);
    godot_dictionary ret = default;
    void** call_args = stackalloc void*[1] { &arg1 };
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(method, ptr, call_args, &ret);
    return Godot.Collections.Dictionary.CreateTakingOwnershipOfDisposableValue(ret);
}
```

The solution taken is to use `NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value` to marshal the return value `godot_dictionary` directly to a hand-written struct that contains the information described in the documentation, see [IntersectRayNonAlloc](https://github.com/Delsin-Yu/tdpl-godot/blob/5327094284e7c77f06f3fb6cb285ea16ce59f3f0/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/NonAlloc.cs#L106)

```csharp
public record struct IntersectRayResult(
    GodotObject Collider,
    long ColliderId,
    Vector2 Normal,
    Vector2 Position,
    Rid Rid,
    long Shape
)
{
    internal static readonly Variant ColliderKey = "collider";
    internal static readonly Variant ColliderIdKey = "collider_id";
    internal static readonly Variant NormalKey = "normal";
    internal static readonly Variant PositionKey = "position";
    internal static readonly Variant RidKey = "rid";
    internal static readonly Variant ShapeKey = "shape";
}

public unsafe IntersectRayResult? IntersectRayNonAlloc(PhysicsRayQueryParameters2D parameters)
{
    var method = MethodBind1;
    var ptr = GodotObject.GetPtr(this);
    var arg1 = GodotObject.GetPtr(parameters);
    ExceptionUtils.ThrowIfNullPtr(ptr);
    godot_dictionary ret = default;
    void** call_args = stackalloc void*[1] { &arg1 };
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(method, ptr, call_args, &ret);
    if (NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_count(ref ret) == 0) return null;
    if (!NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value(ref ret, (godot_variant)IntersectRayResult.ColliderKey.NativeVar, out godot_variant colliderValue).ToBool()
    || !NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value(ref ret, (godot_variant)IntersectRayResult.ColliderIdKey.NativeVar, out godot_variant colliderIdValue).ToBool()
    || !NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value(ref ret, (godot_variant)IntersectRayResult.NormalKey.NativeVar, out godot_variant normalValue).ToBool()
    || !NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value(ref ret, (godot_variant)IntersectRayResult.PositionKey.NativeVar, out godot_variant positionValue).ToBool()
    || !NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value(ref ret, (godot_variant)IntersectRayResult.RidKey.NativeVar, out godot_variant ridValue).ToBool()
    || !NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_try_get_value(ref ret, (godot_variant)IntersectRayResult.ShapeKey.NativeVar, out godot_variant shapeValue).ToBool())
    {
        NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_destroy(ref ret);
        return null;
    }
    var returnValue = new IntersectRayResult(
        VariantUtils.ConvertToGodotObject(colliderValue),
        colliderIdValue.Int,
        normalValue.Vector2,
        positionValue.Vector2,
        ridValue.Rid,
        shapeValue.Int
    );
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_dictionary_destroy(ref ret);
    return returnValue;
}
```

## Method that returns an `Array`

There are two variations of this issue, based on their scenarios:

### Returned array is of fixed length and used to represent dictionary-like data:

Given the following original method:
```csharp
public float[] CastMotion(PhysicsShapeQueryParameters2D parameters)
{
    var method = MethodBind3;
    var ptr = GodotObject.GetPtr(this);
    var arg1 = GodotObject.GetPtr(parameters);
    ExceptionUtils.ThrowIfNullPtr(ptr);
    using godot_packed_float32_array ret = default;
    void** call_args = stackalloc void*[1] { &arg1 };
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(method, ptr, call_args, &ret);
    return Marshaling.ConvertNativePackedFloat32ArrayToSystemArray(ret);
}
```

By the documentation, we know that the method returns a fixed-sized array with length = 2:
```xml
Returns an array with the safe and unsafe proportions (between 0 and 1) of the motion. The safe proportion is the maximum fraction of the motion that can be made without a collision. The unsafe proportion is the minimum fraction of the distance that must be moved for a collision. If no collision is detected a result of <c>[1.0, 1.0]</c> will be returned.
```

The solution taken is to directly marshal the array to a hard-coded struct equivalent, see [CastMotionNonAlloc](https://github.com/Delsin-Yu/tdpl-godot/blob/5327094284e7c77f06f3fb6cb285ea16ce59f3f0/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/NonAlloc.cs#L218)

```csharp
public unsafe CastMotionResult CastMotionNonAlloc(PhysicsShapeQueryParameters3D parameters)
{
    var method = MethodBind3;
    var ptr = GodotObject.GetPtr(this);
    var arg1 = GodotObject.GetPtr(parameters);
    ExceptionUtils.ThrowIfNullPtr(ptr);
    godot_packed_float32_array ret = default;
    void** call_args = stackalloc void*[1] { &arg1 };
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(method, ptr, call_args, &ret);
    if (ret.Size != 2)
    {
        NativeFuncs.godotsharp_packed_float32_array_destroy(ref ret);
        return new CastMotionResult(1.0f, 1.0f);
    }
    var safeValue = ret.Buffer[0];
    var unsafeValue = ret.Buffer[1];
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_packed_float32_array_destroy(ref ret);
    return new CastMotionResult(safeValue, unsafeValue);
}
```

### Returned array has a variable length and contains identical structured values:

Given the following original method:
```csharp
public Array<Vector3> CollideShape(PhysicsShapeQueryParameters3D parameters, int maxResults = 32)
{
    var method = MethodBind4;
    var ptr = GodotObject.GetPtr(this);
    var arg1 = GodotObject.GetPtr(parameters);
    var arg2 = maxResults;
    ExceptionUtils.ThrowIfNullPtr(ptr);
    godot_array ret = default;
    long arg2_in = arg2;
    void** call_args = stackalloc void*[2] { &arg1, &arg2_in };
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(method, ptr, call_args, &ret);
    return new Godot.Collections.Array<Vector2>(Godot.Collections.Array.CreateTakingOwnershipOfDisposableValue(ret));
}
```

The solution taken is to accept an additional `List<Vector2>` here, and fill it with results when directly iterating the native `godot_array` in the method, see [CollideShapeNonAlloc](https://github.com/Delsin-Yu/tdpl-godot/blob/5327094284e7c77f06f3fb6cb285ea16ce59f3f0/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/NonAlloc.cs#L166C24-L166C46)

```csharp
public unsafe void CollideShapeNonAlloc(PhysicsShapeQueryParameters3D parameters, List<Vector3> results, int maxResults = 32)
{
    var method = MethodBind4;
    var ptr = GodotObject.GetPtr(this);
    var arg1 = GodotObject.GetPtr(parameters);
    var arg2 = maxResults;
    ExceptionUtils.ThrowIfNullPtr(ptr);
    godot_array ret = default;
    long arg2_in = arg2;
    void** call_args = stackalloc void*[2] { &arg1, &arg2_in };
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_method_bind_ptrcall(method, ptr, call_args, &ret);
    for (int i = 0; i < ret.Size; i++)
    {
        if (results.Count >= maxResults) break;
        var item = ret.Elements[i];
        if (item.Type != Variant.Type.Vector3) continue;
        results.Add(item.Vector3);
    }
    NativeFuncs.godotsharp_array_destroy(ref ret);
}
```

AI Usage: The author uses an agent to analyze the original PR [6ab1ba6565e11fe08434ddba643fe2ec52f4572a] to identify shared code paths and create an abstraction to reduce boilerplate [b4c587a50b408953c1ededca43b7a892a5d9832d], which is now fully removed in [1b5f6d99b7c228e7a0e5f65ceb255d2af974ff8c]
